# Code owners — who is asked to review a change to each part of the pipeline (Aaron, 2026-10-07).
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches, and a ruleset
# on main can require that owner's approval before the merge. Paths not listed have no owner:
# a change there needs the ruleset's ordinary review, from anyone with write access.
#
# The owned paths are the ones where a wrong change ships a wrong deck to a client without
# any test or gate noticing: the builders, the gate itself, the template shells, the roster
# and the project rules. Later lines win over earlier ones.

/build/              @aburgard-csi
/validation/         @aburgard-csi
/templates/          @aburgard-csi
/clients.md          @aburgard-csi
/CLAUDE.md           @aburgard-csi
/.github/            @aburgard-csi
/scripts/release_launcher.ps1   @aburgard-csi
/scripts/register_watch_task.ps1   @aburgard-csi
/scripts/register_watchdog_task.ps1   @aburgard-csi
